Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:18:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/23] feat(m11-ld85): add the exact constant-coefficient
 polarized step (POL_SOLVER_LD85)

- finding: the native step routes every segment to the implicit trapezoid: check_stiffness evaluates the RK4 amplification 1 + tau + ... with tau = +lambda dl (> 1 for any absorbing segment) on dl_current without the C_CONST factor; 20000 random segments take the trapezoid, observed order 2.0 [SOLID]
- change: POL_SOLVER_LD85 = 1 replaces check_stiffness -> RK4/trapezoid by pol_rte_ld85_step, a port of BlackLightPlus stokes_segment (LD85 solution, j_P and alpha_P rescales, saturation above delta tau 100) followed by stokes_admissible; the 1/(pol_frac + 0.005) renormalisation is skipped on that path; default 0 keeps upstream behaviour
- verify: libraptor_pol_step.so solver 1 against stokes_couple, max relative difference 4.2e-14 over 20000 segments with delta tau 1e-4..30 and Faraday depth 1e-3..300 per segment
---
